1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 Bg7 5. e3 O-O 6. Be2 b6 7. Ne5 Bb7 8. h4 h6 9. O-O c5 10. Bf3 e6 11. Bg3 Nc6 12. Nxc6 Bxc6 13. Be5 Rc8 14. Ne2 Nd7 15. Bxg7 Kxg7 16. g3 Qf6 17. Nf4 Rc7 18. Re1 Rfc8 19. c3 Qf5 20. Qe2 Rd8 21. Rad1 Rcc8 22. Bg2 cxd4 23. exd4 Kh7 24. Bh3 Qf6 25. Qc2 Re8 26. Re3 Kh8 27. Rde1 Nf8 28. Nd3 Nd7 29. f4 a5 30. Ne5 Kg7 31. Qe2 Qd8 32. h5 g5 33. Nxc6 Rxc6 34. f5 Nf8 35. Rf3 Qd6 36. fxe6 Nxe6 37. Qe5+ Qxe5 38. Rxe5 Nc7 39. Rfe3 Rxe5 40. Rxe5 Kf8 41. Kf2 {"White’s game is still preferable but a win is uncertain. While my game was still in progress, Ansell judged correctly that it was going to end in a draw, so he knew that a draw assured him of a tie for first place at least. Had the case been otherwise he might perhaps have played on." Source: WECU bulletin} 1/2-1/2

